    {
      "at": [
        -31,
        -23
      ],
      "id": 20,
      "text": "ATmega8A at the factory clock (internal RC, 1 MHz) as a small real-time clock: Timer2 counts a 32.768 kHz\nwatch crystal on TOSC1 and TOSC2 (AS2) and overflows once a second; in between the chip sleeps in\nPower-save. Each second the LED on PB0 toggles and the terminal shows \"seconds 12\"."
    }
